  "Question": "Given \\(x=1\\) and \\(y=-1\\), find the value of \\((-2x^2y)\\cdot(3xy^2)\\).",
  "Choices": {},
  "Correct Answer": "6",
  "Accepted Answers": [],
  "Unordered Answers": false,
  "Solution": "\\((-2x^2y)\\cdot(3xy^2)=-6x^3y^3\\). Substituting gives \\(-6\\times1\\times(-1)=6\\).\n\nAlternative method 1: Evaluate each factor directly\n\nSince the variable values are given, evaluate each factor directly. Substituting \\(x=1\\) and \\(y=-1\\) gives\n\\[\n-2x^2y=-2\\cdot1^2\\cdot(-1)=2,\n\\]\n\\[\n3xy^2=3\\cdot1\\cdot(-1)^2=3.\n\\]\nTheir product is \\(2\\cdot3=6\\).",
